# Lumbering Laundry: "{2}: Until end of turn, you may look at face-down creatures you don't control any time" (CR 611.2a,
# 708.5). The permission is the player's for the turn: it outlasts the Laundry, and covers a creature turned face down after
# the ability resolved. Turn 1 Bot1 casts the Laundry and two Moxen. Turn 2 Bot2 casts Shatter at it; in response Bot1 pays
# {2} for the ability, which resolves first, and then the Laundry is destroyed. Bot2 then casts Vengeful Creeper face down,
# and Bot1 knows it is the Creeper. On turn 3 it is hidden from Bot1 again (the ruling).

